@description ReaBackground: video or image behind the arrange view
@author aurnik
@version 1.0.1
@changelog
  Loop is a toggle button on the slider row
  Library thumbnails keep the video's aspect ratio instead of letterboxing into 16:9
@provides
  [darwin] reaper_reabackground.dylib https://github.com/aurnik/ReaBackground/releases/download/v$version/$path
  [script main] ReaBackground.lua https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aurnik/ReaBackground/v$version/ReaBackground.lua
@link
  Source repository https://github.com/aurnik/ReaBackground
  Issue tracker https://github.com/aurnik/ReaBackground/issues
@about
  # ReaBackground

  Shows a muted video (synced to the play and edit cursor) or a still image
  behind REAPER's arrange view on macOS. Items, grid, cursors and overlays
  stay on top; the time selection, mute shading and grid lines read as
  shading over the video.

  After installing, restart REAPER, then run the action **ReaBackground.lua**
  (or Extensions > ReaBackground...) to open the settings window. Import a
  video or image with the + tile, click a thumbnail to use it in the current
  project, or the globe icon to make it the default for every project.

  Requirements: macOS 11 or newer, REAPER with Metal rendering enabled,
  ReaImGui (install it from ReaPack) for the settings window.
